<report>
<title>McNemar and exact (Liddell) test for a paired fourfold table</title>

<p><b>Input table:</b></p>
<table>
<tr><td>@{tab_a1:roundu}</td><td>@{tab_b1:roundu}</td></tr>
<tr><td>@{tab_a2:roundu}</td><td>@{tab_b2:roundu}</td></tr>
</table>

<p>Uncorrected Chi<sup>2</sup> = @{chi:roundu} (1 DF)  <pval>@{chi_p:pval}</pval><br />
Yates' continuity corrected Chi<sup>2</sup> = @{yates_chi:roundu} (1 DF)  <pval>@{yates_chi_p:pval}</pval></p>

<p><b>After Liddell (1983):</b><br />
Point estimate of relative risk (R') = @{risk:roundu}</p>

<p><ci>Exact @{pc:round2}% confidence interval = @{from:roundu} to @{to:roundu}</ci></p>

<p>F = @{f:roundu}<br />
<pval>Two sided @{tail_2:pval}</pval></p>
<block name="r_prime"><p><warn>R' is significantly different from unity</warn></p></block>
</report>
